    Count the chain rounds and recheck the object capacities
    
    The trusted planner now counts the rounds of a proximity-test chain from its
    stage list: one batch round, for every stage but the last one epsilon round,
    its fold rounds and one code-switch round, and the last stage's masked-target
    and base rounds; roots and scalars stay message parts. A chain that does not
    fit the reserved rounds is named with its overage, never silently extended.
    The capacity recheck composes the opened-list derivation with the per-object
    account, so the position capacity is checked once over the whole chain.
    Unit tests cover the round counts, the named budget overage and the composed
    recheck.
    
    The production session assembly with the derived parameters is the next step.

